diff --git a/DOCS/man/options.rst b/DOCS/man/options.rst
index 3fed8f062..54bff121d 100644
--- a/DOCS/man/options.rst
+++ b/DOCS/man/options.rst
@@ -7730,6 +7730,33 @@ them.
     st2094-10
         Specifies the contrast (slope) at the knee point. Defaults to 1.0.
 
+``--tone-mapping-metric=<standard|bt2020-itp|bt2020-adaptive|bt2020-rgb|maxrgb-itp|maxrgb-adaptive|maxrgb-rgb>``
+    Selects the brightness metric for renderer-generated dynamic tone mapping.
+    ``standard`` uses libplacebo's normal brightness metric.
+    The three ``bt2020`` modes use MPV-SK's smooth, homogeneous approximation of
+    the selected literal p=1 BT.2020 perceptual coordinate. ``bt2020-itp``
+    applies the metric-derived compression to I while retaining libplacebo's
+    normal conservative ITP chroma processing. ``bt2020-adaptive`` retains
+    progressively more source IPT chroma for saturated pixels while keeping
+    the same metric-derived I coordinate. ``bt2020-rgb`` applies the exact
+    fixed-hue inverse along the linear RGB ray.
+
+    The three ``maxrgb`` modes use per-pixel ``max(R,G,B)`` for both the
+    percentile/average frame statistics that generate the curve and the
+    per-pixel curve lookup. ``maxrgb-itp`` applies the resulting compression
+    to I with conservative chroma processing, ``maxrgb-adaptive`` uses the
+    same adaptive chroma retention, and ``maxrgb-rgb`` applies it exactly
+    along the linear RGB ray.
+
+    These modes are used only for generic, pixel-measured DTM. If tone mapping is
+    inactive, peak measurement is disabled or unavailable, HDR10+ authored
+    mapping is active, or Dolby Vision L1 metadata is selected as the mapping
+    range, the renderer automatically uses ``standard`` for that frame. The
+    requested option and all physical HDR metadata (including MaxCLL, MaxFALL,
+    mastering display data, and Dolby Vision/HDR10+ metadata) are preserved.
+    Dolby Vision reshape/RPU processing alone does not disable these modes.
+    (``--vo=gpu-next`` only)
+
 ``--inverse-tone-mapping``
     If set, allows inverse tone mapping (expanding dynamic range). Can be used
     for upscaling SDR content to HDR, or for making HDR content brighter.
